    {
      "id": "3c93807a-a378-4e31-ad8d-f84fd7beda6b",
      "name": "Start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 328,
        "content": "## Start here\n\nPrepare an evidence packet for a music supervisor to review. The workflow reads cue details from an email body, checks two rights sources, lists gaps, and records the supervisor's decision.\n\nIt does not obtain a licence or prove complete legal clearance. The production write requires an authenticated approval and no gaps in this limited checklist. Keep licensed-rights verification with the responsible supervisor."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fb20ce9f-bfc1-4335-802d-6e9ed94f8dbc",
      "name": "Connect and configure",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        416
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 524,
        "content": "## Connect and configure\n\n1. Connect Gmail and OpenAI. Review the Gmail cue-sheet search. This version accepts one email per execution and reads textPlain or snippet, not the attachment. Separate batches before this workflow.\n2. Replace the work-registration, master-ownership and production example API URLs; select their Header Auth credentials.\n3. Both lookup APIs must return a cues array keyed by cueId. Work records include numeric writerShareTotal and a syncQuote reference. Master records include masterOwner.\n4. Configure the supervisor and coordinator recipients. Select Header Auth on Wait for Supervisor Approval. Your trusted approval service must POST packetId, boolean approved and reviewer to the execution-specific URL.\n5. Select the Drive folder and Audit Log spreadsheet. Use columns packetId, production, risk, approved, requestedApproval, reviewer, reviewedAt, gaps and driveFileId."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "be53d96a-209a-4cdf-957c-59aca9f49b67",
      "name": "Before switching on",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        16,
        1024
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 372,
        "content": "## Before switching on\n\nTest an empty cue list, incomplete writer shares, a missing master owner, a rejected callback and an approved callback with unresolved gaps. Only a matching authenticated approval with zero gaps may reach the production endpoint.\n\nUse sandbox endpoints and inboxes. Failed service calls stop the run; writes do not retry automatically. Inspect previous writes before replaying.\n\nThe wait has no automatic timeout. Monitor waiting executions and cancel abandoned reviews. No external services or licensing evidence are included with this template."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2fec3279-2e45-4a43-a0d8-90620604d7a8",
      "name": "1. Extract cue identifiers from the email body",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        640,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## 1. Extract cue identifiers from the email body\n\nRead one cue email and extract its production name, cue IDs and titles. Validation rejects missing identifiers, duplicate cue IDs and an empty list before any rights lookup.\n\nThe Gmail filter may match emails with attachments, but this workflow does not parse those files. Put the cue details in the body or add a verified attachment-reading stage upstream."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d98b9b97-c22a-4c6b-8a46-8b0ec34b8b71",
      "name": "2. Match rights evidence to each cue",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1760,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## 2. Match rights evidence to each cue\n\nThe two APIs receive the extracted cue list. Their results are matched by cueId. A missing record creates a gap; duplicate records stop the run.\n\nThe checklist asks for writer shares totalling 100, a master owner and a sync-quote reference. CLEAR means this checklist has no gaps; it does not verify every territory, use, term or licence condition."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "55b9c5b4-42ab-40ce-809a-8f68093c7ca2",
      "name": "3. Prepare a review without changing the evidence",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2880,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## 3. Prepare a review without changing the evidence\n\nThe model summarizes the calculated packet. Build Supervisor Review Packet retains the original cues, gaps and packet ID alongside that explanation.\n\nThe email contains the evidence and the execution-specific callback URL. Configure a trusted approval service to authenticate and send the response. Replying to the email alone will not resume the workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3df74ccb-ec1f-4531-ad6b-37ba8dbf97e5",
      "name": "4. Validate the supervisor's decision",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4000,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## 4. Validate the supervisor's decision\n\nWait accepts an authenticated POST. The response must include the matching packetId, boolean approved and a reviewer identifier. Invalid responses stop the run.\n\nAn approval request cannot override unresolved gaps: approved stays false when the checklist contains gaps. The false path asks the rights coordinator for follow-up; the true path records the approved packet in your production system."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
